    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d976">

                <pb facs="1021" n="1009" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/12–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-01T00:00:00-04:00">January 1,
                            1945—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Re your 11374, December 22, 1944.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d976-f1"/> Please
                    inform Foreign Office that detailed proposals for establishment of a direct
                    radiotelegraph circuit between the United States and Saudi Arabia will shortly
                    be made to the Saudi Arabian Government and obtain definite assurances that
                    British Government will interpose no objection to establishment of such a
                    circuit and operation of a radiotelegraph station by Saudi Government provided
                    adequate censorship arrangements are agreed upon by the British, American and
                    Saudi Governments.</p>
                <p>Please endeavor to obtain above assurances at earliest possible date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
